.SH NAME
dh_installnuget \- install NuGet packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBdh_installnuget\fR [\fIdebhelper\ options\fR] [\fB\-\-nuget\-path=\fR\fIpath\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBdh_installnuget\fR installs NuGet packages to system-wide locations.
.PP
By default, packages are installed to \fI/usr/lib/nuget/\fR.
Use \fB\-\-nuget\-path\fR to specify a custom installation path.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
.IP "debian/\fIpackage\fR.nuget debian/nuget" 4
.IX Item "debian/package.nuget debian/nuget"
Lists the NuGet packages to be installed per package. Each line in that file
should be of the form \f(CW\*(C`\fR\f(CIpath\fR\f(CW\*(C'\fR, where \fIpath\fR indicates where the NuGet
package resides in the source tree.
.SH OPTIONS
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
.IP \fB\-\-nuget\-path=\fR\fIpath\fR 4
.IX Item "--nuget-path=path"
Set the base installation path. Can be specified only once.
When used, the default path is \fBnot\fR used.
.Sp
Default (when no \-\-nuget\-path specified): \fI/usr/lib/nuget/\fR
.Sp
Example:
  \-\-nuget\-path=/usr/share/nuget
.SH NOTES
.IX Header "NOTES"
Note that this command is not idempotent. \fBdh_prep\fR\|(1) should be called
between invocations of this command. Otherwise, it may cause multiple
instances of the same text to be added to maintainer scripts.
.PP
When using custom paths (especially \fI/usr/local\fR), be aware that this may
violate Debian Policy and could cause issues with package management. Consider
using standard paths like \fI/usr/share\fR or \fI/usr/lib\fR for official packages.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBdebhelper\fR\|(7)
.PP
This program is not a part of debhelper.
